---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';

const title = `About | ${SITE_TITLE}`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<header class="page-header">
				<h1>About West Michigan Politics</h1>
				<p class="hero-lead">{SITE_DESCRIPTION}</p>
			</header>

			<div class="prose">
				<h2>Mission</h2>
				<p>
					We focus on Holland and Ottawa County first, then the wider lakeshore region—helping
					residents understand who represents them and what their elected officials are doing in
					their name.
				</p>

				<h2>Editorial standards</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Balance:</strong> Legislator profiles separate "what supporters highlight" from
						"what critics raise." We do not present one side as objective fact.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Sources:</strong> Factual claims link to primary documents, official statements,
						or reputable local/national reporting. We correct errors when verified.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Clarity:</strong> We avoid jargon where plain language works. When legislative
						text matters, we summarize impact for local readers.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Independence:</strong> This site is not affiliated with any party, campaign, or
						officeholder. Profiles are research-based, not paid promotion.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>How we stay even-handed</h2>
				<p>
					Even-handedness is structural here, not aspirational. Every current officeholder gets the
					identical profile skeleton — track record, supporter highlights, critic concerns,
					community submissions, coverage, and sources — and gaps render as visible "not yet
					documented" notes instead of quietly disappearing. Profiles receive an editorial score
					only after at least two sourced points are documented on each side. Our{' '}
					<a href="/coverage/">coverage dashboard</a> shows exactly where reporting is thin, so you
					can hold us to the same standard we hold officeholders.
				</p>

				<h2>What we are not</h2>
				<p>
					We are not a substitute for legal advice, official casework, or emergency services. For
					help with a federal agency, contact your representative's office directly. For voting
					districts and ballots, use Michigan's official voter tools.
				</p>

				<h2>Contact & corrections</h2>
				<p>
					Spotted an error or have a sourced addition? Email{' '}
					<a href="mailto:corrections@wmpolitics.com">corrections@wmpolitics.com</a> with a link to
					the claim and your source, or use the submission form on any legislator profile. We review
					every correction and update the page (with a note) when it checks out.
				</p>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
